yes(545,'D','The reaction produces chlorine: MnO₂ + 4HCl → MnCl₂ + Cl₂ + 2H₂O. Chlorine is used in water disinfection because it destroys many disease-causing microorganisms.',[RX,REB],question='Oxidation of concentrated hydrochloric acid with manganese(IV) oxide produces a gas used in',options=['Manufacturing toothpaste','Treating simple goitre','Vulcanising rubber','Disinfecting water'],audit='Replaced inaccurate sterilization term with disinfection and repaired spelling; same intended chlorine application.',check='chlorine-balance')
yes(546,'C','The concentration equilibrium expression places products above reactants, with each concentration raised to its stoichiometric coefficient. Thus Kc = [G]ᵖ[H]ᑫ / ([E]ᵐ[F]ⁿ).',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/13-2-equilibrium-constants'],question='For mE + nF ⇌ pG + qH, which is the concentration equilibrium expression, with each species included as a concentration term?',options=['[E]ᵐ[F]ⁿ / ([G]ᵖ[H]ᑫ)','[E][F] / ([G][H])','[G]ᵖ[H]ᑫ / ([E]ᵐ[F]ⁿ)','[G][H] / ([E][F])'],audit='Restored four fraction bars and exponents directly from PDF48.')
